Z||000000||fierofreek2001||04-08-2001||09:57 PM||||hey list, this is another subwoofer question for you all..<BR>has anyone mounted a 10" subwoofer in a custom box where a stock fiero subwoofer would go?  is this even POSSIBLE!?!?  the reason i want to know is i decided that the floor sub was just getting in the passengers way too much and it was time to find another alternative ... im not a behind the seat fan, and i hear bad things about subs in the front compartment.. <BR>well if this is possible , let me know!<BR>steve<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||04-08-2001||10:05 PM||||A 10" sub in the stock location is not possible from what I can tell. It's just too big. An 8" will fit though. I think Josh (TheFiero64) has a setup with an 8" sub in the stock location. You should talk to him about it.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily overheating)||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||04-08-2001||10:43 PM||||Talk to Stoic (forum member)<P>he has one, I've seen it.. didn't get to hear it though.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||04-09-2001||12:04 AM||||A decent 10" in the stock location would have to be a "free-air" type of speaker. You cannont get the amount of volume required for a sealed or ported box using a regular speaker. I am building an 8" sub into the stock location and getting the correct volume for that is proving to be tight at best.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierofreek2001||04-09-2001||06:55 PM||||well has anyone ever made an enclosure for the area under the dash for an 8" sub?   open air just doesnt really impress me much.. the bass just isnt there that way..||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||04-09-2001||11:54 PM||||What do you mean by "under the dash?"<P>Are you still talking about the stock location or...???||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||04-10-2001||12:08 AM||||I am in the process of building an "under-dash" box to house an 8" woofer. It will fill the area where the stock sub was. So far the design requires movement of the "dingy thingy"  But it looks like I can fit a .39 cu ft box under there. The speaker I have chosen requires .30 minimum. Many 8" fall between .3 and .4 cu ft. If things go well, it'll look stock and be unseen from the outside window. I should have everything finalized by this weekend. (building the box this week)<BR>This will be a sealed box. There is no way to get a properly ported box up there.<BR>All drawings will be posted along with exact measurements of the box.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||TheFiero64||04-10-2001||04:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B>A 10" sub in the stock location is not possible from what I can tell. It's just too big. An 8" will fit though. I think Josh (TheFiero64) has a setup with an 8" sub in the stock location. You should talk to him about it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep, an 8 inch just fits. A ten would be too big to fit.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
